    {
      "slug": "call",
      "kind": "sequence",
      "why": "Every call stops at one decision (allow, ask or deny) before any connector runs, so the picture is the order of that call, not boxes.",
      "label": "How one tool call runs. An AI app sends tools/call to the gateway, which verifies the token and hands the call to the service. The service asks the Authorizer, which answers allow, ask or deny. On ask the app gets pending_approval and the call waits for a person. On allow the service calls the connector runtime with the credential, gets a filtered result back and answers the app; the event goes to the outbox in the same transaction.",
      "actors": [
